// shader-differential - fixture for a FILE-SCOPE CONST (t_4584aa27).
//
// The reference compiler folds the constant's value inline AND adds a
// parameter entry named K listing the code offsets where the value sits;
// ours folds it without the parameter.  The director retired the plan for
// a flag over "promote vs fold" (2026-09-01 22:24): the instructions are the
// same either way, so promotion is container metadata, not a lowering, and
// there is nothing to compare at draw time.  What this fixture guards is
// the FOLD ITSELF: the release dropped the initialiser and compiled K as
// zero on both paths (t_4584aa27, fixed in 0981daa).  One row, set 0,
// both paths: ours vs the reference, no uniform applied, identical since
// the fix.
//
// Channels are chosen so each mechanism is visible on its own channel:
//   R  uv.x * K   K reaching a varying product (level count > 1)
//   G  K          the constant itself, one level whose 8-bit value IS the
//                 default (0.3125 -> 80); a zero default reads 0 here
//   B  uv.y * K   the other varying axis, same product
//   A  1
// K = 0.3125 = 5/16 is exact in float32.
const float K = 0.3125;

float4 main(float2 uv : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR
{
    return float4(uv.x * K, K, uv.y * K, 1.0);
}
